{"audio": "luke-16.opus", "duration_ms": 266951, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2060, "end_ms": 3560, "text": "Luke, Chapter Sixteen."}, {"start_ms": 5300, "end_ms": 12241, "text": "Jesus also said to His disciples, “There was a rich man whose manager was accused of wasting his possessions."}, {"start_ms": 12681, "end_ms": 15941, "text": "So he called him in to ask, ‘What is this I hear about you?"}, {"start_ms": 16361, "end_ms": 27581, "text": "Turn in an account of your management, for you cannot be manager any longer.’ The manager said to himself, ‘What shall I do, now that my master is taking away my position?"}, {"start_ms": 28361, "end_ms": 31141, "text": "I am too weak to dig and too ashamed to beg."}, {"start_ms": 32001, "end_ms": 41642, "text": "I know what I will do so that after my removal from management, people will welcome me into their homes.’ And he called in each one of his master’s debtors."}, {"start_ms": 42242, "end_ms": 44702, "text": "‘How much do you owe my master?’ he asked the first."}, {"start_ms": 45242, "end_ms": 47482, "text": "‘A hundred measures of olive oil,’ he answered."}, {"start_ms": 48042, "end_ms": 58082, "text": "‘Take your bill,’ said the manager, ‘sit down quickly, and write fifty.’ Then he asked another, ‘And how much do you owe?’ ‘A hundred measures of wheat,’ he replied."}, {"start_ms": 58782, "end_ms": 61143, "text": "‘Take your bill and write eighty,’ he told him."}, {"start_ms": 62223, "end_ms": 66603, "text": "The master commended the dishonest manager because he had acted shrewdly."}, {"start_ms": 67423, "end_ms": 72783, "text": "For the sons of this age are more shrewd in dealing with their own kind than are the sons of light."}, {"start_ms": 73363, "end_ms": 80963, "text": "I tell you, use worldly wealth to make friends for yourselves so that when it is gone, they will welcome you into eternal dwellings."}, {"start_ms": 81643, "end_ms": 90644, "text": "Whoever is faithful with very little will also be faithful with much, and whoever is dishonest with very little will also be dishonest with much."}, {"start_ms": 91364, "end_ms": 96984, "text": "So if you have not been faithful with worldly wealth, who will entrust you with true riches?"}, {"start_ms": 97684, "end_ms": 102884, "text": "And if you have not been faithful with the belongings of another, who will give you belongings of your own?"}, {"start_ms": 103884, "end_ms": 105884, "text": "No servant can serve two masters."}, {"start_ms": 106464, "end_ms": 111945, "text": "Either he will hate the one and love the other, or he will be devoted to the one and despise the other."}, {"start_ms": 112525, "end_ms": 121565, "text": "You cannot serve both God and money.” The Pharisees, who were lovers of money, heard all of this and were scoffing at Jesus."}, {"start_ms": 122265, "end_ms": 128885, "text": "So He said to them, “You are the ones who justify yourselves before men, but God knows your hearts."}, {"start_ms": 129485, "end_ms": 133045, "text": "For what is prized among men is detestable before God."}, {"start_ms": 133806, "end_ms": 136726, "text": "The Law and the Prophets were proclaimed until John."}, {"start_ms": 137406, "end_ms": 144186, "text": "Since that time, the gospel of the kingdom of God is being preached, and everyone is forcing his way into it."}, {"start_ms": 144986, "end_ms": 151086, "text": "But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for a single stroke of a pen to drop out of the Law."}, {"start_ms": 152326, "end_ms": 159647, "text": "Anyone who divorces his wife and marries another woman commits adultery, and he who marries a divorced woman commits adultery."}, {"start_ms": 160827, "end_ms": 166427, "text": "Now there was a rich man dressed in purple and fine linen, who lived each day in joyous splendor."}, {"start_ms": 167067, "end_ms": 175367, "text": "And a beggar named Lazarus lay at his gate, covered with sores and longing to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man’s table."}, {"start_ms": 176267, "end_ms": 178647, "text": "Even the dogs came and licked his sores."}, {"start_ms": 179927, "end_ms": 184128, "text": "One day the beggar died and was carried by the angels to Abraham’s side."}, {"start_ms": 184948, "end_ms": 187228, "text": "And the rich man also died and was buried."}, {"start_ms": 188068, "end_ms": 195468, "text": "In Hades, where he was in torment, he looked up and saw Abraham from afar, with Lazarus by his side."}, {"start_ms": 196388, "end_ms": 204648, "text": "So he cried out, ‘Father Abraham, have mercy on me and send Lazarus to dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue."}, {"start_ms": 205108, "end_ms": 216269, "text": "For I am in agony in this fire.’ But Abraham answered, ‘Child, remember that during your lifetime you received your good things, while Lazarus received bad things."}, {"start_ms": 216849, "end_ms": 219929, "text": "But now he is comforted here, while you are in agony."}, {"start_ms": 220729, "end_ms": 236270, "text": "And besides all this, a great chasm has been fixed between us and you, so that even those who wish cannot cross from here to you, nor can anyone cross from there to us.’ ‘Then I beg you, father,’ he said, ‘send Lazarus to my father’s house,"}, {"start_ms": 236650, "end_ms": 238250, "text": "for I have five brothers."}, {"start_ms": 238750, "end_ms": 254670, "text": "Let him warn them, so that they will not also end up in this place of torment.’ But Abraham replied, ‘They have Moses and the Prophets; let your brothers listen to them.’ ‘No, father Abraham,’ he said, ‘but if someone is sent to them from the dead,"}, {"start_ms": 254871, "end_ms": 264771, "text": "they will repent.’ Then Abraham said to him, ‘If they do not listen to Moses and the Prophets, they will not be persuaded even if someone rises from the dead.’”"}], "words": [{"t": "Luke,", "s": 2060, "e": 2300, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2660, "e": 3000, "si": 0}, {"t": "Sixteen.", "s": 3080, "e": 3560, "si": 0}, {"t": "J